    <p class="lede">Most American homes leak 30–50% more air than the code now requires for new construction. That leakage shows up directly in your heating and cooling bills, and indirectly in every HVAC quote you get — because a leaky envelope demands a bigger heat pump, furnace, or AC than the same house would need if sealed. This guide explains how air sealing is measured, what professional sealing actually addresses, when DIY makes sense, and the combustion-safety rule that matters.</p>
